# Project Documentation

**Project Name:** Exploring Marathon Trends  
**Author:** Kimberly Blodgett  
**Purpose:** Analyze marathon participation and performance trends using publicly available race data.

## Datasets

- `2023_results.csv` – Finish results for 2023 marathons  
- `2023_race.csv` – Race information for 2023  
- `2024_results.csv` – Finish results for 2024 marathons  
- `2024_race.csv` – Race information for 2024  
- `boston_men.csv` – Boston Marathon winners (Men)  
- `boston_women.csv` – Boston Marathon winners (Women)  

## Analysis Overview

### Participation Trends
- Top 20 races by finishers (2023 vs 2024)  
- Gender distribution (Men vs Women; Non-Binary/Other <0.1%)  

### Performance Trends
- Overall average finish times by year  
- Average finish times by gender  
- Boston Marathon winners over time (Men vs Women; women raced from 1972)  
- Finish time spread by age and gender (shows variability)  
- Comparison of top 10% finishers vs amateurs  

### Race Popularity
- Top 10 races highlighted using color gradients for visualization  

## Tools & Libraries
- **Python:** pandas, matplotlib, seaborn  
- **Jupyter Notebook:** `notebooks/analysis.ipynb`
